      "title": "Surface disjoint union preserves multiplicity but lacks Carrier coproduct legs",
      "status": "established_for_explicit_bare_surface_operation_graph",
      "demonstrated_strength": [
        "unbounded mapping-class groupoid theorem",
        "source-typed finite operation audit"
      ],
      "body": "For the bare surface statements in entries 7, 10, and 46, actual disjoint union preserves connected-component multiplicity: in the mapping-class groupoid generated by a connected U, U^{sqcup m} is isomorphic to U^{sqcup n} only when m=n. But this groupoid has no morphism U -> U sqcup U, and the separating cut Delta_C has source the connected parent Sigma rather than either component. Hence the explicitly established coefficient-neutral operation graph contains zero of the two component-injection legs needed for a coproduct, with typed deficit 2. Commutative R-algebras would supply unit-dependent factor maps into a tensor coproduct only after crossing to a coefficient lens. Thus monoidal addition is a positive candidate, while the Phase-I categorical-coproduct gate remains unpassed.",
      "entity_id": "claim:a71b26d80103a048bd3e"
    },
