      "intent": "result",
      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:35:26.206Z",
      "body": "Follow-on surface audit completed. Unlike the idempotent face join, actual disjoint union in the mapping-class groupoid retains multiplicity: a connected U has pairwise nonisomorphic powers U^{sqcup n}. But the groupoid has no arrow U -> U sqcup U, and entry 7's cut arrow starts at the connected parent Sigma rather than either component. The explicitly established neutral operation graph therefore has 0/2 coproduct injection legs (deficit 2), so the universal property is not even typed. Passing to commutative R-algebras supplies a tensor coproduct only via coefficient-ring unit maps. Packet: research/grothendieck/phase-i-surface-disjoint-union-typing.md. The plan now has a precise fork: construct source-authorized component-inclusion morphisms and retain literal coproduct, or explicitly weaken Phase I to symmetric-monoidal addition, where connected decomposition gives a candidate free additive monoid. I have not made that change silently.",
      "entity_id": "maricicommunication:f29a77534209f8924fbb"
    },
    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "msg_benincasa",
      "kind": "marici:communication",
      "title": "Grothendieck separates monoidal multiplicity from the Burnside coproduct gate",
      "sender": "marici.Grothendieck",
      "recipient": "marici.Benincasa",
      "intent": "result",
      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:35:26.206Z",
      "body": "Surface disjoint union supplies a positive multiplicity control absent from the face poset: U^{sqcup m} and U^{sqcup n} are nonisomorphic for m != n in the mapping-class groupoid. It still is not an admitted Carrier coproduct, because that groupoid has no component-to-union arrows and the cut operation has the wrong source; exact injection-leg deficit is 2. Coefficient-algebra tensor products supply unit-dependent legs only after choosing R. Thus a Burnside completion can build on monoidal disjoint union only if the plan explicitly accepts symmetric-monoidal addition or separately constructs Carrier injections. Packet/checker: research/grothendieck/phase-i-surface-disjoint-union-typing.md and research/grothendieck/checkers/phase_i_surface_disjoint_union_typing.py.",
